preConditionHook:
// PAST THE FIRST HOUR, THE DAY IS A TREND DAY. The close has broken beyond
// the opening range by at least breakMultiple times that range's OWN height,
// so treat the day as a trend day and take only with-trend entries for the
// rest of it. Short is the mirror below the opening range low.
//
// The candidate's own note is honest that Brooks's trend-day test is pattern
// recognition; the opening-range break scaled by the range's own height is
// the proxy, and it is the one measurable statement the two sources share.
//
// NOT OpeningRangeBreakout, which fires on the bare close beyond the level:
// at breakMultiple = 0 this rule reproduces that one at firstCrossOnly = 0,
// and the whole content here is the BUFFER, sized to the opening range
// itself, so a wide opening range demands a proportionally larger break. The
// two are kept apart the way ConsecutiveUpBars and StrongTrendBarRun are --
// the degenerate setting exists, but the general rule is a different claim
// and the base rule keeps reproducing bit for bit.
//
// Kept apart from SessionTrendDayDirection, which measures from the
// session's opening price against an ATR: on a wide-range opening the two
// disagree, and they should be tested against each other before either is
// trusted. Kept apart
// from OpeningRangeVsAvgDailyRange, which only measures the opening range's
// WIDTH and never asks whether price left it.
//
// SessionOpeningRange is INLINED rather than referenced, per the composites
// decision, in the same spelling OpeningRangeBreakout uses: the bar on which
// barsIn reaches firstHourBars is still part of the range and its own high is
// already in orHigh, so the test is >= firstHourBars and the first bar that
// can fire is firstHourBars + 1.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision: the twin's date > date[1],
// mirrored as day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)); barsIn is 1 on the
// session's first bar. WARM-UP mirrors EL: barsIn, orHigh and orLow hold
// their initial 0 if the first calculated bar falls mid-session, so orLow
// stays 0.0 until the first date change and the short side cannot fire.
// Intraday bars only.
//
// Deepest bar touched: 1.
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    barsIn = 1;
    orHigh = high[0];
    orLow = low[0];
} else {
    barsIn = barsIn + 1;
    if (barsIn <= (int)firstHourBars) {
        if (el_gt(high[0], orHigh)) orHigh = high[0];
        if (el_lt(low[0], orLow)) orLow = low[0];
    }
}
trendUp = el_ge((double)barsIn, firstHourBars) && el_gt(close[0], orHigh + breakMultiple * (orHigh - orLow));
trendDn = el_ge((double)barsIn, firstHourBars) && el_lt(close[0], orLow - breakMultiple * (orHigh - orLow));
